## Free Tier Limits
Spark plan gives 10K Functions invocations, 360MB outbound data, and Firestore quotas that support ~1K daily users without hitting paywalls. OpenAI costs extra (~$0.15/1M input tokens on gpt-4o-mini), but Functions keep API keys server-side. Upgrade to Blaze only if chats explode past free quotas.[12][7]

## Firebase Setup
1. Create project at console.firebase.google.com (pick Spark).
2. Enable Hosting, Firestore (test mode for dev), Functions.
3. Install Firebase CLI: `npm install -g firebase-tools`, login, init in your project folder.[11]

## Backend: Proxy Function
Create `functions/index.js` to call OpenAI securely—no client-side key exposure:

```javascript
const functions = require('firebase-functions');
const { Configuration, OpenAIApi } = require('openai');

const config = new Configuration({ apiKey: functions.config().openai.key });
const openai = new OpenAIApi(config);

exports.chat = functions.https.onCall(async (data, context) => {
  const { message } = data;
  const systemPrompt = `You are a sarcastic Cape Coloured ou from Cape Town, speaking lekker slang like "aweh", "sies", "bru", "ag shame". Answer casual but informative.`;

  try {
    const completion = await openai.createChatCompletion({
      model: 'gpt-4o-mini',
      messages: [
        { role: 'system', content: systemPrompt },
        { role: 'user', content: message }
      ],
    });
    return { reply: completion.data.choices[0].message.content };
  } catch (error) {
    return { error: 'Sies, something vrot happened bru' };
  }
});
```

Set secret: `firebase functions:config:set openai.key="your-key"`, deploy: `firebase deploy`.[13]

## Frontend Hosting
Use your earlier HTML/JS, replace direct fetch with Firebase SDK:

```html
<script type="module">
  import { initializeApp } from 'https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.11.0/firebase-app.js';
  import { getFunctions, httpsCallable } from 'https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.11.0/firebase-functions.js';

  const firebaseConfig = { /* Your config from Firebase console */ };
  const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);
  const functions = getFunctions(app);

  async function sendMessage(userMsg) {
    const chat = httpsCallable(functions, 'chat');
    const result = await chat({ message: userMsg });
    displayMessage(result.data.reply, 'incoming');
